            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch fixes a double release of data space on failed direct IO copy-on-write (COW) writes in the Btrfs file system. The issue occurs when a COW write fails after reserving data space, causing the reserved extent to be freed and then releasing all allocated data space again. This results in an underflow of available data space, leading to warnings and clamping to zero. The patch records the consumed length during reservation and releases only the remaining allocated data space on error, preventing the double release and fixing the issue.",
